                                   }
                     },
                     {
                         "version":  "0.7.1",
                         "date":  "2026-03-26",
                         "stage":  "Beta",
                         "notes":  "New: Nightscout CGM Support (v0.7.0)\r\n  - Added Nightscout as a third CGM provider alongside Dexcom Share and LibreLinkUp\r\n  - Enter your Nightscout server URL and optional API token to receive glucose readings\r\n  - Supports both HTTP and HTTPS — HTTP connections use zero TLS memory\r\n  - URLs without a protocol prefix automatically default to HTTPS\r\n  - Full UI with login flow, keyboard entry, and password masking for API tokens\r\n\r\n  Fix: Device Stability\r\n  - Eliminated overnight freeze caused by LVGL shadow rendering stack overflow\r\n  - Always close SSL after each glucose fetch — ensures every cycle starts with clean contiguous heap\r\n  - Increased glucose task stack from 4KB to 5KB to prevent NVS save stack overflow\r\n  - Added breathing heartbeat dot between home screen cards — visual indicator the device is alive\r\n  - Fixed provider switch login failures (Dexcom/Libre/Nightscout) on fragmented heap\r\n  - Fixed power off button failing on fragmented heap\r\n  - Fixed OTA auto-install button failing silently on fragmented heap\r\n\r\n  Fix: Nightscout HTTPS\r\n  - Fixed TLS handshake failure with Cloudflare-hosted Nightscout instances (SNI was disabled)\r\n  - Optimized status endpoint validation — no longer parses full JSON response\r\n  - Reduced HTTP response buffer to 2KB (glucose responses are only ~230 bytes)\r\n\r\n  Other\r\n  - SD serial logging now disabled by default — users get clean glucose CSV only\r\n  - New ship serial command for factory reset + power off (for shipping fresh devices)\r\n  - New log on / log off serial commands to toggle debug logging\r\n  - CGM provider dispatch refactored from bool to enum for cleaner three-provider support\r\n  - Serial command listener now starts even without SD card",
                         "files":  {
                                       "merged":  "firmware/v0.7.1/cygm-merged.bin",
